# Customizing the {{ project_upper }} solver

Generated by dendrosym. This is your map of the **handful of places you'd ever
hand-edit**. The guiding rule:

> **You regenerate only three things** — the RHS kernels, the constraint kernels,
> and the (analytic) initial data — and you do that by editing the solver
> **config** and re-running the generator, *not* by editing generated C++.
> Everything else below is either a runtime knob (TOML) or a clearly-marked hook.

---

## 1. Tuning a run — no rebuild of generation
Edit `{{ project_name }}_parameters.sample.toml` (copy it per run). Resolution,
domain, CFL, IO/checkpoint frequency, refinement mode, RK type, BH params, etc.
are all here. Defaults live in `solver/src/parameters.cpp`.

## 2. Initial data
`solver/src/grUtils.cpp` -> `initDataFuncToPhysCoords()` switches on
`{{ project_upper }}_ID_TYPE` (set in TOML). To add your own:
forward-declare a function, add a `case`, implement it. (Analytic IC defined in
the config is regenerated; non-analytic/raw IC is hand-added here.)

## 3. RHS / constraint kernels  — REGENERATE, don't hand-edit
The generated kernels (`solver/gencode/*.cpp.inc`, wired in `rhs.cpp` /
`physcon.cpp`) come from the equations in your solver **config** (e.g.
`{{ project_name }}.py`). Change the physics there and regenerate. Hand-edits to
generated kernels are overwritten on the next run.

## 4. Evolution loop — cadence & custom diagnostics
`solver/{{ project_name }}_main.cpp`, the `while (ets->curr_time() < time_end)`
loop. Safe to edit: add custom output, change what runs how often, add
post-processing. The framework machinery around it (mesh build, workspace, dt,
remesh) is abstracted into dendrolib and should not need touching.

## 5. Per-step / per-stage hooks  (empty stubs, meant for you)
`solver/src/{{ project_upper }}Ctx.cpp`:
- `pre_stage` / `post_stage` / `pre_timestep` / `post_timestep` (and the `_blk`
  variants) — return-0 stubs. Fill them for custom monitoring, dissipation,
  per-stage adjustments, etc.

## 6. Two non-obvious knobs
- **Initial-data constraint enforcement:** `{{ project_upper }}Ctx::init_grid()`
  calls `enforce_{{ project_name }}_constraints(...)`. This cleans the raw IC to
  satisfy the constraints. Optional — remove the call if you want the raw IC.
- **Refinement criterion:** `{{ project_upper }}_REFINEMENT_MODE` (TOML) selects
  it; the logic is `{{ project_upper }}Ctx::is_remesh()`. Edit there only for a
  custom criterion.

---
*If you find yourself editing anything not in this list, it probably belongs in
the generator (the config) or in dendrolib (the framework) — ask before
hand-patching generated framework code, since it won't survive regeneration.*
